  "revision_note": [
    "v1 is kept in nav-gold-v1.json and both scores are reported in",
    "nav-results.md. v1 listed only the class a test names. Re-reading the",
    "source showed that was wrong about the mechanism, not just incomplete:",
    "every 'cache[1] = 1' dispatches to Cache.__setitem__ on the base class,",
    "_TimedCache holds the _Timer that the timed caches call, 'func.cache_info()'",
    "is a direct call into _cached.cache_info, and bad_choice is a local",
    "function the test hands in and the cache then invokes. All of that is",
    "code under test by any honest reading, so v2 adds it.",
    "The correction was made after seeing v0.2 output. It raises precision,",
    "so it is reported alongside v1 rather than replacing it silently."
  ],
  "method": [
    "Read each test body by hand and record the definitions whose behaviour the",
    "test asserts on. Production code, inherited base classes and test-local",
    "helpers all count, because all three run. The test function itself and its",
    "own TestCase class do not count.",
    "Entries the navigator is expected to miss are kept in. Removing them would",
    "inflate recall and hide the real limits of name-based resolution."
  ],
